/-
# Cassels, Chapter 10, Example 2: the action of $O^+(\Lambda_p)$ on the vectors of value $p^{-1}$

**Layer** (as in `Example1.lean` and `Ch11Sec3Local.lean`): $V_\mathfrak p = F_\mathfrak p^3$ at a finite prime
$\mathfrak p \nmid 2$ of a number field $F$ (Cassels: $\mathbb Q_p$, $p \ne 2$), $Q$ = `Q : QuadForm F 3`, a lattice $L$
and its localization $\Lambda_p = L_\mathfrak p$ = `loc v L.1` with basis the columns of $\gamma$, Gram matrix
`locGram Q v γ` of $B(x,y) = Q(x+y)-Q(x)-Q(y)$; $\theta$ = `spinorNorm`; $\mathfrak p\Lambda_p$ = `pLat v L`.

**Proves** (Cassels, *Rational Quadratic Forms*, Ch. 10, Example 2, p. 192): in the setting of Example 1 (integer-valued
form on $\Lambda_p$, determinant of valuation exactly $1$) suppose also that $V_\mathfrak p$ is anisotropic, let
$b \in \Lambda_p$ with $\lvert Q(b)\rvert = \lvert\varpi\rvert$ and $\sigma \in O^+(\Lambda_p)$. Then
$\sigma b \equiv \varepsilon b \pmod{\mathfrak p\Lambda_p}$ with $\varepsilon = +1$ if $\theta(\sigma)$ is a unit class and
$\varepsilon = -1$ if $\theta(\sigma)$ is the class of $\varpi$ times a unit (`ch10_example2`). The statement is proved
for every $\sigma \in O(\Lambda_p)$ (`ch10_example2_orth`); the hypothesis $\det\sigma = 1$ is not needed.
Generalization: a number field $F$ in place of $\mathbb Q$.

**Proof** (not Cassels' sketch through a list of primitive symmetries). (1) Diagonalize (`exists_diag_basis`): an
orthogonal basis $e_i, e_j, e_k$ with $\lvert Q(e_i)\rvert = \lvert Q(e_j)\rvert = 1$, $\lvert Q(e_k)\rvert = \lvert\varpi\rvert$.
(2) Anisotropy and Hensel's lemma: if $x = x_ie_i + x_je_j + x_ke_k \in \Lambda_p$ has $x_i$ or $x_j$ a unit, then $Q(x)$ is
a unit. Hence a vector $b$ of value $\lvert\varpi\rvert$ has $x_i, x_j \in \mathfrak p$, $x_k$ a unit, and
$B(b, y) \in \mathfrak p$ for all $y \in \Lambda_p$. (3) $O(\Lambda_p)$ is generated by the symmetries $\tau_z$,
$z \in \Lambda_p$ with $Q(z)$ a unit, together with $\tau_{e_k}$ (`DiagFrame.mem_closure`: two steps of the
fixing argument of `exists_fix_step`, in a variant that fixes the unit vectors first). (4) On the generators:
$\tau_z b \equiv b$ and $\tau_{e_k} b \equiv -b$; and $\theta(\tau_z)$ is a unit class while $\theta(\tau_{e_k})$ is not.
(5) The set of $\sigma$ that act on the vectors of value $\lvert\varpi\rvert$ as $\varepsilon$ with $\varepsilon = 1$ exactly
when $\theta(\sigma)$ is a unit class is a subgroup, so it contains $O(\Lambda_p)$.
-/
import QuadFormsKB.Literature.Cassels.Ch11Sec3Local

open NumberField IsDedekindDomain Matrix WithZero

set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false

noncomputable section

namespace QuadFormsKB.Lattices

variable {F : Type} [Field F] [NumberField F] (v : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 F))

local notation "Fv" => v.adicCompletion F
local notation "𝔬" => v.adicCompletionIntegers F

/-! ### The lattice $\mathfrak p\Lambda_p$ and valuation helpers -/

section PLat

variable {n : ℕ}

/-- **$\mathfrak p\Lambda_p$**, the product of the maximal ideal of $\mathfrak o_\mathfrak p$ and the localization
$\Lambda_p = L_\mathfrak p$ of the lattice `L : Lat F n` at the prime `v`: the set of $\varpi y$ with $y \in L_\mathfrak p$ and
$\varpi$ the uniformizer `LocalDensity.NF.π v` (the set does not depend on the choice of uniformizer). -/
def pLat (L : Lat F n) : Set (Fin n → Fv) :=
  {x | ∃ y ∈ loc v L.1, x = ((LocalDensity.NF.π v : 𝔬) : Fv) • y}

variable {v}

/-- Helper: the uniformizer has valuation $\exp(-1)$ in the completion; in particular it is nonzero. -/
theorem valued_pi : Valued.v ((LocalDensity.NF.π v : 𝔬) : Fv) = exp (-1 : ℤ) :=
  LocalDensity.NF.valued_π v

/-- Helper: the uniformizer `LocalDensity.NF.π v` is nonzero in the completion. -/
theorem pi_ne_zero : ((LocalDensity.NF.π v : 𝔬) : Fv) ≠ 0 := fun h => by
  have := valued_pi (v := v)
  rw [h, map_zero] at this
  exact WithZero.exp_ne_zero this.symm

/-- Helper: a scalar of valuation $\le 1$ acts on $L_\mathfrak p$. -/
theorem smul_mem_loc (L : Lat F n) {s : Fv} (hs : Valued.v s ≤ 1) {y : Fin n → Fv} (hy : y ∈ loc v L.1) :
    s • y ∈ loc v L.1 :=
  (loc v L.1).smul_mem (⟨s, (HeightOneSpectrum.mem_adicCompletionIntegers _ _ _).mpr hs⟩ : 𝔬) hy

/-- Helper: $0 \in \mathfrak p L_\mathfrak p$. -/
theorem zero_mem_pLat (L : Lat F n) : (0 : Fin n → Fv) ∈ pLat v L :=
  ⟨0, (loc v L.1).zero_mem, (smul_zero _).symm⟩

/-- Helper: $\mathfrak p L_\mathfrak p$ is closed under addition. -/
theorem add_mem_pLat (L : Lat F n) {x y : Fin n → Fv} (hx : x ∈ pLat v L) (hy : y ∈ pLat v L) :
    x + y ∈ pLat v L := by
  obtain ⟨a, ha, rfl⟩ := hx
  obtain ⟨b, hb, rfl⟩ := hy
  exact ⟨a + b, (loc v L.1).add_mem ha hb, (smul_add _ _ _).symm⟩

/-- Helper: $\mathfrak p L_\mathfrak p$ is closed under negation. -/
theorem neg_mem_pLat (L : Lat F n) {x : Fin n → Fv} (hx : x ∈ pLat v L) : -x ∈ pLat v L := by
  obtain ⟨a, ha, rfl⟩ := hx
  exact ⟨-a, (loc v L.1).neg_mem ha, (smul_neg _ _).symm⟩

/-- Helper: $\mathfrak p L_\mathfrak p$ is closed under subtraction. -/
theorem sub_mem_pLat (L : Lat F n) {x y : Fin n → Fv} (hx : x ∈ pLat v L) (hy : y ∈ pLat v L) :
    x - y ∈ pLat v L := by
  rw [sub_eq_add_neg]; exact add_mem_pLat L hx (neg_mem_pLat L hy)

/-- Helper: $\mathfrak p L_\mathfrak p$ is closed under scalars of valuation $\le 1$. -/
theorem smul_mem_pLat (L : Lat F n) {s : Fv} (hs : Valued.v s ≤ 1) {x : Fin n → Fv} (hx : x ∈ pLat v L) :
    s • x ∈ pLat v L := by
  obtain ⟨a, ha, rfl⟩ := hx
  exact ⟨s • a, smul_mem_loc L hs ha, smul_comm _ _ _⟩

/-- Helper: $c\,y \in \mathfrak p\Lambda_p$ for $y \in \Lambda_p$ and $\lvert c\rvert \le \lvert\varpi\rvert$. -/
theorem smul_mem_pLat_of_le (L : Lat F n) {c : Fv} (hc : Valued.v c ≤ exp (-1 : ℤ)) {y : Fin n → Fv}
    (hy : y ∈ loc v L.1) : c • y ∈ pLat v L := by
  have hπ := valued_pi (v := v)
  have hc' : Valued.v (c / ((LocalDensity.NF.π v : 𝔬) : Fv)) ≤ 1 := by
    rw [map_div₀, hπ, div_le_one₀ (by simp)]; exact hc
  refine ⟨(c / ((LocalDensity.NF.π v : 𝔬) : Fv)) • y, smul_mem_loc L hc' hy, ?_⟩
  rw [smul_smul, mul_div_cancel₀ _ pi_ne_zero]

/-- Helper: an element of $\mathbb Z\cup\{-\infty\}$-valued group with value $< 1$ has value $\le \exp(-1)$. -/
theorem exp_neg_one_bound_of_lt_one {w : WithZero (Multiplicative ℤ)} (hw : w < 1) : w ≤ exp (-1 : ℤ) := by
  rcases eq_or_ne w 0 with rfl | h0
  · exact bot_le
  · obtain ⟨m, rfl⟩ : ∃ m : ℤ, w = exp m := ⟨WithZero.log w, (exp_log h0).symm⟩
    rw [← exp_zero, exp_lt_exp] at hw
    rw [exp_le_exp]; omega

end PLat

/-! ### Unit square classes and the parity of the valuation -/

section SqParity

variable {v}

/-- Helper: the square class of the unit $x$ of $F_\mathfrak p$ as `sqClassOf`. -/
theorem sqClassOf_units (x : Fvˣ) : sqClassOf (x : Fv) = SqClass.mk x := by
  rw [sqClassOf_of_ne_zero x.ne_zero]
  exact congrArg SqClass.mk (Units.ext rfl)

/-- Helper: the class of $x \in F_\mathfrak p^\times$ is a unit class exactly when $\operatorname{ord}_\mathfrak p x$ is
even. -/
theorem isUnitSqClass_mk_iff (x : Fvˣ) :
    IsUnitSqClass v (SqClass.mk x) ↔ Even (WithZero.log (Valued.v (x : Fv))) := by
  have hx0 : Valued.v (x : Fv) ≠ 0 := (Valuation.ne_zero_iff _).mpr x.ne_zero
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨u, hu, hmk⟩
    have hu0 : u ≠ 0 := fun h => by rw [h, map_zero] at hu; exact zero_ne_one hu
    have hc : sqClassOf ((x : Fv) * u) = 1 := by
      rw [sqClassOf_mul x.ne_zero hu0, ← hmk, sqClassOf_units]
      exact SqClass.mul_self _
    obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := (sqClassOf_eq_one_iff (mul_ne_zero x.ne_zero hu0)).mp hc
    have hr0 : Valued.v r ≠ 0 := by
      intro h
      have : r = 0 := (Valuation.zero_iff _).mp h
      rw [this, mul_zero] at hr
      exact mul_ne_zero x.ne_zero hu0 hr
    have h1 : Valued.v (x : Fv) = Valued.v r * Valued.v r := by
      have := congrArg Valued.v hr
      rwa [map_mul, hu, mul_one, map_mul] at this
    refine ⟨WithZero.log (Valued.v r), ?_⟩
    rw [h1]
    conv_lhs => rw [← exp_log hr0]
    rw [← exp_add, log_exp]
  · rintro ⟨m, hm⟩
    have hv : Valued.v (x : Fv) = exp (m + m) := by rw [← hm, exp_log hx0]
    have hπ := valued_pi (v := v)
    refine ⟨(x : Fv) * (((LocalDensity.NF.π v : 𝔬) : Fv) ^ m) ^ 2, ?_, ?_⟩
    · rw [map_mul, map_pow, map_zpow₀, hπ, hv, ← WithZero.exp_zsmul, ← WithZero.exp_nsmul, ← exp_add, ← exp_zero,
        exp_inj]
      simp only [smul_eq_mul, nsmul_eq_mul]
      push_cast
      ring
    · rw [sqClassOf_mul x.ne_zero (pow_ne_zero 2 (zpow_ne_zero _ pi_ne_zero)),
        (sqClassOf_eq_one_iff (pow_ne_zero 2 (zpow_ne_zero _ pi_ne_zero))).mpr ⟨_, sq _⟩, mul_one,
        sqClassOf_units]

/-- Helper: the class of $w \ne 0$ is a unit class exactly when $\operatorname{ord}_\mathfrak p w$ is even. -/
theorem isUnitSqClass_sqClassOf_iff {w : Fv} (hw : w ≠ 0) :
    IsUnitSqClass v (sqClassOf w) ↔ Even (WithZero.log (Valued.v w)) := by
  rw [sqClassOf_of_ne_zero hw, isUnitSqClass_mk_iff]
  rfl

/-- Helper: a product of two square classes is a unit class exactly when both or neither factor is. -/
theorem isUnitSqClass_mul_iff (c d : SqClass Fv) :
    IsUnitSqClass v (c * d) ↔ (IsUnitSqClass v c ↔ IsUnitSqClass v d) := by
  induction c using SqClass.ind with
  | h x =>
    induction d using SqClass.ind with
    | h y =>
      rw [← SqClass.mk_mul, isUnitSqClass_mk_iff, isUnitSqClass_mk_iff, isUnitSqClass_mk_iff, Units.val_mul,
        map_mul, WithZero.log_mul ((Valuation.ne_zero_iff _).mpr x.ne_zero)
          ((Valuation.ne_zero_iff _).mpr y.ne_zero), Int.even_add]

/-- Helper: a unit class is not the class of a uniformizer times a unit. -/
theorem not_isUnitSqClass_uniformizer_mul {u : Fv} (hu : Valued.v u = 1) :
    ¬ IsUnitSqClass v (sqClassOf (((LocalDensity.NF.π v : 𝔬) : Fv) * u)) := by
  have hu0 : u ≠ 0 := fun h => by rw [h, map_zero] at hu; exact zero_ne_one hu
  rw [isUnitSqClass_sqClassOf_iff (mul_ne_zero pi_ne_zero hu0), map_mul, hu, mul_one, valued_pi, log_exp]
  decide

/-- Helper: every square class is either a unit class or the class of a uniformizer times a unit. -/
theorem isUnitSqClass_or_uniformizer (c : SqClass Fv) :
    IsUnitSqClass v c ∨ ∃ u : Fv, Valued.v u = 1 ∧ c = sqClassOf (((LocalDensity.NF.π v : 𝔬) : Fv) * u) := by
  induction c using SqClass.ind with
  | h x =>
    by_cases he : IsUnitSqClass v (SqClass.mk x)
    · exact Or.inl he
    · right
      have hπ := valued_pi (v := v)
      rw [isUnitSqClass_mk_iff] at he
      have hx0 : Valued.v (x : Fv) ≠ 0 := (Valuation.ne_zero_iff _).mpr x.ne_zero
      have hw0 : (x : Fv) / ((LocalDensity.NF.π v : 𝔬) : Fv) ≠ 0 := div_ne_zero x.ne_zero pi_ne_zero
      have hev : Even (WithZero.log (Valued.v ((x : Fv) / ((LocalDensity.NF.π v : 𝔬) : Fv)))) := by
        rw [map_div₀, hπ]
        have e : Valued.v (x : Fv) / exp (-1 : ℤ) = exp (WithZero.log (Valued.v (x : Fv)) - (-1)) := by
          rw [exp_sub, exp_log hx0]
        rw [e, log_exp, sub_neg_eq_add]
        exact (Int.not_even_iff_odd.mp he).add_one
      obtain ⟨u, hu, hmk⟩ := (isUnitSqClass_sqClassOf_iff hw0).mpr hev
      refine ⟨u, hu, ?_⟩
      have hu0 : u ≠ 0 := fun h => by rw [h, map_zero] at hu; exact zero_ne_one hu
      rw [sqClassOf_mul pi_ne_zero hu0, ← hmk, ← sqClassOf_mul pi_ne_zero (div_ne_zero x.ne_zero pi_ne_zero),
        mul_div_cancel₀ _ pi_ne_zero, sqClassOf_units]

end SqParity

/-! ### Hensel's lemma for a binary unit form -/

section Hensel

variable {v}

/-- Helper: **Hensel for a binary form** ($\mathfrak p \nmid 2$). If $a, b, x, y$ are units of $\mathfrak o_\mathfrak p$ and
$\lvert ax^2 + by^2\rvert < 1$, then $a + bz^2 = 0$ for some $z \in F_\mathfrak p$ (the residue of $-a/b$ is the square of the
residue of $y/x$, and a unit of $\mathfrak o_\mathfrak p$ whose residue is a nonzero square is a square). -/
theorem exists_zero_of_unit_binary (h2 : (2 : 𝓞 F) ∉ v.asIdeal) {a b x y : Fv} (ha : Valued.v a = 1)
    (hb : Valued.v b = 1) (hx : Valued.v x = 1) (hy : Valued.v y = 1)
    (hs : Valued.v (a * x ^ 2 + b * y ^ 2) < 1) : ∃ z : Fv, a + b * z ^ 2 = 0 := by
  have hπ := LocalDensity.NF.irreducible_π v
  have hπ2 := LocalDensity.NF.π_not_dvd_two v h2
  have ne0 : ∀ {w : Fv}, Valued.v w = 1 → w ≠ 0 := fun hw h => by
    rw [h, map_zero] at hw; exact zero_ne_one hw
  have hb0 := ne0 hb
  have hx0 := ne0 hx
  have hc1 : Valued.v (-a / b) ≤ 1 := by rw [map_div₀, Valuation.map_neg, ha, hb]; simp
  have hyx : Valued.v (y / x) = 1 := by rw [map_div₀, hy, hx]; simp
  set c : 𝔬 := toO v (-a / b) hc1 with hc
  set t : 𝔬 := toO v (y / x) hyx.le with ht
  have htu : IsUnit t := HeightOneSpectrum.adicCompletionIntegers.isUnit_iff_valued_eq_one.mpr hyx
  have hres : IsLocalRing.residue 𝔬 c = (IsLocalRing.residue 𝔬 t) ^ 2 := by
    rw [← sub_eq_zero, ← map_pow, ← map_sub, IsLocalRing.residue_eq_zero_iff, IsLocalRing.mem_maximalIdeal,
      mem_nonunits_iff]
    intro hu
    have h1 := HeightOneSpectrum.adicCompletionIntegers.isUnit_iff_valued_eq_one.mp hu
    have e : (((c - t ^ 2 : 𝔬)) : Fv) = -(a * x ^ 2 + b * y ^ 2) / (b * x ^ 2) := by
      show -a / b - (y / x) ^ 2 = _
      field_simp
      ring
    rw [e, map_div₀, Valuation.map_neg, map_mul, hb, map_pow, hx] at h1
    simp only [one_mul, one_pow, div_one] at h1
    exact absurd h1 hs.ne
  obtain ⟨z0, hz0⟩ := Nbr.exists_sq_eq_of_residue hπ hπ2 c
    (by rw [Ne, IsLocalRing.residue_eq_zero_iff, IsLocalRing.mem_maximalIdeal, mem_nonunits_iff, not_not]; exact htu)
    hres
  refine ⟨(z0 : Fv), ?_⟩
  have : ((z0 ^ 2 : 𝔬) : Fv) = -a / b := congrArg (fun w : 𝔬 => (w : Fv)) hz0
  have h' : (z0 : Fv) ^ 2 = -a / b := this
  rw [h']
  field_simp
  ring

end Hensel

/-! ### A diagonal frame and the consequences of anisotropy -/

section DiagFrame

variable (Q : QuadForm F 3)

/-- Helper: **a diagonal frame of $L_\mathfrak p$.** The columns $e_a = \gamma\,\mathrm{single}_a$ ($a \in \{0,1,2\}$) of
`γ` form an orthogonal basis of `loc v L.1` for the bilinear form of `Q` (`orth`), and the three indices `i`, `j`, `k`
are distinct with $\lvert B(e_i,e_i)\rvert = \lvert B(e_j,e_j)\rvert = 1$ and $\lvert B(e_k,e_k)\rvert = \lvert\varpi\rvert$
(`vi`, `vj`, `vk`). -/
structure DiagFrame (L : Lat F 3) (γ : GL (Fin 3) Fv) (i j k : Fin 3) : Prop where
  basis : loc v L.1 = locAct v γ (std v)
  orth : ∀ a b, a ≠ b → locGram Q v γ a b = 0
  ij : i ≠ j
  ik : i ≠ k
  jk : j ≠ k
  vi : Valued.v (locGram Q v γ i i) = 1
  vj : Valued.v (locGram Q v γ j j) = 1
  vk : Valued.v (locGram Q v γ k k) = exp (-1 : ℤ)

variable {Q v} {L : Lat F 3} {γ : GL (Fin 3) (v.adicCompletion F)} {i j k : Fin 3}

/-- Helper: the three indices of a frame exhaust `Fin 3`. -/
theorem DiagFrame.cases (hF : DiagFrame v Q L γ i j k) (a : Fin 3) : a = i ∨ a = j ∨ a = k := by
  have h1 := hF.ij
  have h2 := hF.ik
  have h3 := hF.jk
  clear hF
  revert i j k a
  decide

/-- Helper: a sum over `Fin 3` is the sum over the three indices of a frame. -/
theorem DiagFrame.sum3 (hF : DiagFrame v Q L γ i j k) {M : Type*} [AddCommMonoid M] (f : Fin 3 → M) :
    ∑ a, f a = f i + f j + f k := by
  have hu : (Finset.univ : Finset (Fin 3)) = {i, j, k} := by
    ext a; simp only [Finset.mem_univ, Finset.mem_insert, Finset.mem_singleton, true_iff]; exact hF.cases a
  rw [hu, Finset.sum_insert (by simp [hF.ij, hF.ik]), Finset.sum_insert (by simp [hF.jk]), Finset.sum_singleton,
    add_assoc]

/-- Helper: the bilinear form on coordinates of a frame:
$B(\gamma d, \gamma d') = \sum_a B(e_a,e_a)\,d_a d'_a$. -/
theorem DiagFrame.qbil_eq (hF : DiagFrame v Q L γ i j k) (d d' : Fin 3 → Fv) :
    qbil Q Fv (γ.val *ᵥ d) (γ.val *ᵥ d') =
      locGram Q v γ i i * (d i * d' i) + locGram Q v γ j j * (d j * d' j) + locGram Q v γ k k * (d k * d' k) := by
  rw [qbil_mulVec_locGram, dotProduct, hF.sum3]
  simp only [locGram_mulVec_diag hF.orth]
  ring

/-- Helper: $B(e_i,e_i) \ne 0$. -/
theorem DiagFrame.ne_zero_i (hF : DiagFrame v Q L γ i j k) : locGram Q v γ i i ≠ 0 := fun h => by
  have := hF.vi; rw [h, map_zero] at this; exact zero_ne_one this

/-- Helper: $B(e_j,e_j) \ne 0$. -/
theorem DiagFrame.ne_zero_j (hF : DiagFrame v Q L γ i j k) : locGram Q v γ j j ≠ 0 := fun h => by
  have := hF.vj; rw [h, map_zero] at this; exact zero_ne_one this

/-- Helper: $B(e_k,e_k) \ne 0$. -/
theorem DiagFrame.ne_zero_k (hF : DiagFrame v Q L γ i j k) : locGram Q v γ k k ≠ 0 := fun h => by
  have := hF.vk; rw [h, map_zero] at this; exact WithZero.exp_ne_zero this.symm

/-- Helper: $\gamma d \in L_\mathfrak p$ for $d \in \mathfrak o_\mathfrak p^3$. -/
theorem DiagFrame.mem_loc (hF : DiagFrame v Q L γ i j k) {d : Fin 3 → Fv} (hd : d ∈ std v) : γ.val *ᵥ d ∈ loc v L.1 := by
  rw [hF.basis]; exact ⟨d, hd, rfl⟩

/-- Helper: the basis vector $e_a$ lies in $L_\mathfrak p$. -/
theorem DiagFrame.single_mem (hF : DiagFrame v Q L γ i j k) (a : Fin 3) : γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single a 1 ∈ loc v L.1 :=
  hF.mem_loc (single_mem_std a (by simp))

/-- Helper: $Q(e_k) \ne 0$. -/
theorem DiagFrame.eval_ne_zero_k (hF : DiagFrame v Q L γ i j k) : Q.evalIn Fv (γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single k 1) ≠ 0 := by
  intro h
  have h1 := two_mul_evalIn_eq Q Fv (γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single k 1)
  rw [locGram_apply_eq, h, mul_zero] at h1
  exact hF.ne_zero_k h1.symm

/-- Helper: a bound for $\lvert c\,w^2\rvert$. -/
theorem val_mul_sq_le {c w : Fv} {m : ℤ} (hc : Valued.v c ≤ exp m) (hw : Valued.v w ≤ exp (-1 : ℤ)) :
    Valued.v (c * w ^ 2) ≤ exp (m - 2) := by
  rw [map_mul, map_pow]
  calc Valued.v c * Valued.v w ^ 2 ≤ exp m * exp (-1 : ℤ) ^ 2 := mul_le_mul' hc (pow_le_pow_left' hw 2)
    _ = exp (m - 2) := by
      rw [← WithZero.exp_nsmul, ← exp_add]; rfl

/-- Helper: a bound for $\lvert c\,(a b)\rvert$. -/
theorem val_mul_mul_le {c a b : Fv} {C A B : WithZero (Multiplicative ℤ)} (hc : Valued.v c ≤ C)
    (ha : Valued.v a ≤ A) (hb : Valued.v b ≤ B) : Valued.v (c * (a * b)) ≤ C * (A * B) := by
  rw [map_mul, map_mul]; exact mul_le_mul' hc (mul_le_mul' ha hb)

/-- Helper: **anisotropy and Hensel.** If $x = \gamma d \in L_\mathfrak p$ has the $e_i$- or the $e_j$-coordinate a unit,
then $Q(x)$ is a unit: otherwise $Q(e_i d_i + e_j d_j)$ would have value in $\mathfrak p$ with unit coordinates, and Hensel's
lemma (`exists_zero_of_unit_binary`) would produce an isotropic vector $e_i + ze_j$. -/
theorem DiagFrame.eval_unit (hF : DiagFrame v Q L γ i j k) (h2 : (2 : 𝓞 F) ∉ v.asIdeal)
    (hint : ∀ x ∈ loc v L.1, Valued.v (Q.evalIn Fv x) ≤ 1) (haniso : ¬ Q.IsotropicIn Fv) {d : Fin 3 → Fv}
    (hd : d ∈ std v) (hu : Valued.v (d i) = 1 ∨ Valued.v (d j) = 1) :
    Valued.v (Q.evalIn Fv (γ.val *ᵥ d)) = 1 := by
  by_contra hne
  have hd' := mem_std_iff.mp hd
  have h2v := valued_two h2
  have hlt := lt_of_le_of_ne (hint _ (hF.mem_loc hd)) hne
  have hexp : exp (-1 : ℤ) < (1 : WithZero (Multiplicative ℤ)) := by rw [← exp_zero, exp_lt_exp]; omega
  have key : 2 * Q.evalIn Fv (γ.val *ᵥ d) = locGram Q v γ i i * d i ^ 2 + locGram Q v γ j j * d j ^ 2 +
      locGram Q v γ k k * d k ^ 2 := by
    rw [two_mul_evalIn_eq, hF.qbil_eq]; ring
  set t : Fv := locGram Q v γ k k * d k ^ 2 with ht
  have hk : Valued.v t < 1 := by
    refine lt_of_le_of_lt ?_ hexp
    rw [ht, map_mul, hF.vk, map_pow]
    calc exp (-1 : ℤ) * Valued.v (d k) ^ 2 ≤ exp (-1 : ℤ) * 1 := mul_le_mul' le_rfl (pow_le_one' (hd' k) 2)
      _ = _ := mul_one _
  have hs : Valued.v (locGram Q v γ i i * d i ^ 2 + locGram Q v γ j j * d j ^ 2) < 1 := by
    have : locGram Q v γ i i * d i ^ 2 + locGram Q v γ j j * d j ^ 2 = 2 * Q.evalIn Fv (γ.val *ᵥ d) + -t := by
      rw [key, ht]; ring
    rw [this]
    refine Valuation.map_add_lt _ ?_ (by rw [Valuation.map_neg]; exact hk)
    rw [map_mul, h2v, one_mul]; exact hlt
  have hdi : Valued.v (d i) = 1 := by
    by_contra hi
    have hi' : Valued.v (d i) < 1 := lt_of_le_of_ne (hd' i) hi
    have hdj : Valued.v (d j) = 1 := hu.resolve_left hi
    have h1 : Valued.v (locGram Q v γ i i * d i ^ 2) < 1 := by
      rw [map_mul, hF.vi, one_mul, map_pow]; exact pow_lt_one' hi' two_ne_zero
    have h2' : Valued.v (locGram Q v γ j j * d j ^ 2) = 1 := by
      rw [map_mul, hF.vj, map_pow, hdj]; simp
    have := Valuation.map_add_eq_of_lt_right _ (h1.trans_eq h2'.symm)
    rw [this, h2'] at hs
    exact lt_irrefl _ hs
  have hdj : Valued.v (d j) = 1 := by
    by_contra hj
    have hj' : Valued.v (d j) < 1 := lt_of_le_of_ne (hd' j) hj
    have h1 : Valued.v (locGram Q v γ j j * d j ^ 2) < 1 := by
      rw [map_mul, hF.vj, one_mul, map_pow]; exact pow_lt_one' hj' two_ne_zero
    have h2' : Valued.v (locGram Q v γ i i * d i ^ 2) = 1 := by
      rw [map_mul, hF.vi, map_pow, hdi]; simp
    have := Valuation.map_add_eq_of_lt_left _ (h1.trans_eq h2'.symm)
    rw [this, h2'] at hs
    exact lt_irrefl _ hs
  obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ := exists_zero_of_unit_binary h2 hF.vi hF.vj hdi hdj hs
  set c : Fin 3 → Fv := Pi.single i 1 + z • Pi.single j 1 with hc
  have hci : c i = 1 := by simp [hc, hF.ij]
  have hcj : c j = z := by simp [hc, hF.ij.symm]
  have hck : c k = 0 := by simp [hc, hF.ik.symm, hF.jk.symm]
  have hne0 : c ≠ 0 := fun h => by have := congrFun h i; rw [hci] at this; simp at this
  have hγ0 : (γ.val *ᵥ c) ≠ 0 := fun h =>
    hne0 (Matrix.eq_zero_of_mulVec_eq_zero (Matrix.isUnits_det_units γ).ne_zero h)
  refine haniso ⟨γ.val *ᵥ c, hγ0, ?_⟩
  apply mul_left_cancel₀ (two_ne_zero : (2 : Fv) ≠ 0)
  rw [two_mul_evalIn_eq, hF.qbil_eq, hci, hcj, hck]
  linear_combination hz

/-- Helper: **the coordinates of a vector of value $\lvert\varpi\rvert$.** If $b = \gamma d \in L_\mathfrak p$ has
$\lvert Q(b)\rvert = \lvert\varpi\rvert$, then $d_i, d_j \in \mathfrak p$ and $d_k$ is a unit. -/
theorem DiagFrame.coords (hF : DiagFrame v Q L γ i j k) (h2 : (2 : 𝓞 F) ∉ v.asIdeal)
    (hint : ∀ x ∈ loc v L.1, Valued.v (Q.evalIn Fv x) ≤ 1) (haniso : ¬ Q.IsotropicIn Fv) {d : Fin 3 → Fv}
    (hd : d ∈ std v) (hb : Valued.v (Q.evalIn Fv (γ.val *ᵥ d)) = exp (-1 : ℤ)) :
    Valued.v (d i) ≤ exp (-1 : ℤ) ∧ Valued.v (d j) ≤ exp (-1 : ℤ) ∧ Valued.v (d k) = 1 := by
  have hd' := mem_std_iff.mp hd
  have h2v := valued_two h2
  have hne1 : exp (-1 : ℤ) ≠ (1 : WithZero (Multiplicative ℤ)) := fun h => by
    rw [← exp_zero, exp_inj] at h; omega
  refine ⟨exp_neg_one_bound_of_lt_one (lt_of_le_of_ne (hd' i) fun h => hne1 ?_),
    exp_neg_one_bound_of_lt_one (lt_of_le_of_ne (hd' j) fun h => hne1 ?_), ?_⟩
  · rw [← hb]; exact hF.eval_unit h2 hint haniso hd (Or.inl h)
  · rw [← hb]; exact hF.eval_unit h2 hint haniso hd (Or.inr h)
  by_contra hk
  have hi : Valued.v (d i) ≤ exp (-1 : ℤ) := by
    refine exp_neg_one_bound_of_lt_one (lt_of_le_of_ne (hd' i) fun h => hne1 ?_)
    rw [← hb]; exact hF.eval_unit h2 hint haniso hd (Or.inl h)
  have hj : Valued.v (d j) ≤ exp (-1 : ℤ) := by
    refine exp_neg_one_bound_of_lt_one (lt_of_le_of_ne (hd' j) fun h => hne1 ?_)
    rw [← hb]; exact hF.eval_unit h2 hint haniso hd (Or.inr h)
  have hk' := exp_neg_one_bound_of_lt_one (lt_of_le_of_ne (hd' k) hk)
  have key : 2 * Q.evalIn Fv (γ.val *ᵥ d) = locGram Q v γ i i * d i ^ 2 + locGram Q v γ j j * d j ^ 2 +
      locGram Q v γ k k * d k ^ 2 := by
    rw [two_mul_evalIn_eq, hF.qbil_eq]; ring
  have hle : Valued.v (2 * Q.evalIn Fv (γ.val *ᵥ d)) ≤ exp (-2 : ℤ) := by
    rw [key]
    refine Valuation.map_add_le _ (Valuation.map_add_le _ ?_ ?_) ?_
    · simpa using val_mul_sq_le (m := 0) (le_of_eq (by rw [hF.vi, exp_zero])) hi
    · simpa using val_mul_sq_le (m := 0) (le_of_eq (by rw [hF.vj, exp_zero])) hj
    · exact (val_mul_sq_le (m := -1) (le_of_eq hF.vk) hk').trans (exp_le_exp.mpr (by omega))
  rw [map_mul, h2v, one_mul, hb, exp_le_exp] at hle
  omega

/-- Helper: $B(e_a, \gamma d) = B(e_a,e_a)\,d_a$ for the orthogonal basis vector $e_a$. -/
theorem qbil_single_eq {γ : GL (Fin 3) Fv} (horth : ∀ a b, a ≠ b → locGram Q v γ a b = 0) (a : Fin 3)
    (d : Fin 3 → Fv) :
    qbil Q Fv (γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single a 1) (γ.val *ᵥ d) = locGram Q v γ a a * d a := by
  rw [qbil_mulVec_locGram, single_dotProduct, one_mul, locGram_mulVec_diag horth]

/-- Helper: **$B(b, y) \in \mathfrak p$** for a vector $b$ of value $\lvert\varpi\rvert$ and every $y \in L_\mathfrak p$. -/
theorem DiagFrame.bil_le (hF : DiagFrame v Q L γ i j k) {d d' : Fin 3 → Fv} (hd' : d' ∈ std v)
    (hi : Valued.v (d i) ≤ exp (-1 : ℤ)) (hj : Valued.v (d j) ≤ exp (-1 : ℤ)) (hk : Valued.v (d k) = 1) :
    Valued.v (qbil Q Fv (γ.val *ᵥ d) (γ.val *ᵥ d')) ≤ exp (-1 : ℤ) := by
  rw [hF.qbil_eq]
  have hd'' := mem_std_iff.mp hd'
  refine Valuation.map_add_le _ (Valuation.map_add_le _ ?_ ?_) ?_
  · simpa using val_mul_mul_le (le_of_eq hF.vi) hi (hd'' i)
  · simpa using val_mul_mul_le (le_of_eq hF.vj) hj (hd'' j)
  · simpa using val_mul_mul_le (le_of_eq hF.vk) (le_of_eq hk) (hd'' k)

/-- Helper: a vector as the combination of the three basis vectors of a frame. -/
theorem DiagFrame.decomp (hF : DiagFrame v Q L γ i j k) (d : Fin 3 → Fv) :
    γ.val *ᵥ d = d i • (γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single i 1) + d j • (γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single j 1) +
      d k • (γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single k 1) := by
  have hd : d = d i • (Pi.single i 1 : Fin 3 → Fv) + d j • (Pi.single j 1 : Fin 3 → Fv) +
      d k • (Pi.single k 1 : Fin 3 → Fv) := by
    ext a
    rcases hF.cases a with rfl | rfl | rfl
    · simp [hF.ij, hF.ik]
    · simp [hF.ij.symm, hF.jk]
    · simp [hF.ik.symm, hF.jk.symm]
  conv_lhs => rw [hd]
  simp only [Matrix.mulVec_add, Matrix.mulVec_smul]

/-! ### The action on vectors of value $\lvert\varpi\rvert$ -/

variable (Q v L)

/-- Helper: **$\sigma$ acts as the scalar $s$ on the vectors of value $\lvert\varpi\rvert$ modulo $\mathfrak p\Lambda_p$**:
$\sigma b - s\,b \in \mathfrak p L_\mathfrak p$ for every $b \in L_\mathfrak p$ with $\lvert Q(b)\rvert = \lvert\varpi\rvert$. -/
def ActsAs (σ : orthGroup Q Fv) (s : Fv) : Prop :=
  ∀ b ∈ loc v L.1, Valued.v (Q.evalIn Fv b) = exp (-1 : ℤ) →
    (σ : GL (Fin 3) Fv).val *ᵥ b - s • b ∈ pLat v L

variable {Q v L}

/-- Helper: elements of $O(L_\mathfrak p)$ map $L_\mathfrak p$ into itself. -/
theorem mulVec_mem_loc {σ : orthGroup Q Fv} (hσ : σ ∈ locStabV Q v L) {y : Fin 3 → Fv} (hy : y ∈ loc v L.1) :
    (σ : GL (Fin 3) Fv).val *ᵥ y ∈ loc v L.1 := by
  have hσ' : locAct v (σ : GL (Fin 3) Fv) (loc v L.1) = loc v L.1 := hσ
  rw [← hσ']
  exact mem_locAct.mpr ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩

/-- Helper: elements of $O(L_\mathfrak p)$ map $\mathfrak p L_\mathfrak p$ into itself. -/
theorem mulVec_mem_pLat {σ : orthGroup Q Fv} (hσ : σ ∈ locStabV Q v L) {x : Fin 3 → Fv} (hx : x ∈ pLat v L) :
    (σ : GL (Fin 3) Fv).val *ᵥ x ∈ pLat v L := by
  obtain ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩ := hx
  exact ⟨_, mulVec_mem_loc hσ hy, Matrix.mulVec_smul _ _ _⟩

/-- Helper: if $\sigma$ acts as $s$ and $\tau$ as $t$ ($\lvert t\rvert \le 1$), then $\sigma\tau$ acts as $st$. -/
theorem ActsAs.mul {σ τ : orthGroup Q Fv} (hσ : σ ∈ locStabV Q v L) {s t : Fv} (ht : Valued.v t ≤ 1)
    (hs' : ActsAs v Q L σ s) (ht' : ActsAs v Q L τ t) : ActsAs v Q L (σ * τ) (s * t) := by
  intro b hb hQb
  have e : ((σ * τ : orthGroup Q Fv) : GL (Fin 3) Fv).val *ᵥ b - (s * t) • b =
      (σ : GL (Fin 3) Fv).val *ᵥ ((τ : GL (Fin 3) Fv).val *ᵥ b - t • b) +
        t • ((σ : GL (Fin 3) Fv).val *ᵥ b - s • b) := by
    rw [coe_mul_mulVec, Matrix.mulVec_sub, Matrix.mulVec_smul]
    module
  rw [e]
  exact add_mem_pLat L (mulVec_mem_pLat hσ (ht' b hb hQb)) (smul_mem_pLat L ht (hs' b hb hQb))

/-- Helper: if $\sigma$ acts as $s$ with $s^2 = 1$ and $\lvert s\rvert \le 1$, then so does $\sigma^{-1}$. -/
theorem ActsAs.inv {σ : orthGroup Q Fv} (hσ : σ ∈ locStabV Q v L) {s : Fv} (hs : s * s = 1)
    (hs1 : Valued.v s ≤ 1) (h : ActsAs v Q L σ s) : ActsAs v Q L σ⁻¹ s := by
  intro b hb hQb
  have hinv : ((σ⁻¹ : orthGroup Q Fv) : GL (Fin 3) Fv).val *ᵥ ((σ : GL (Fin 3) Fv).val *ᵥ b) = b := by
    rw [← coe_mul_mulVec, inv_mul_cancel]; simp
  have e : ((σ⁻¹ : orthGroup Q Fv) : GL (Fin 3) Fv).val *ᵥ b - s • b =
      (-s) • ((σ⁻¹ : orthGroup Q Fv) : GL (Fin 3) Fv).val *ᵥ
        ((σ : GL (Fin 3) Fv).val *ᵥ b - s • b) := by
    rw [Matrix.mulVec_sub, Matrix.mulVec_smul, hinv]
    funext a
    simp only [Pi.sub_apply, Pi.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul]
    linear_combination (-(((σ⁻¹ : orthGroup Q Fv) : GL (Fin 3) Fv).val *ᵥ b) a) * hs
  rw [e]
  refine smul_mem_pLat L (by rw [Valuation.map_neg]; exact hs1) ?_
  exact mulVec_mem_pLat ((locStabV Q v L).inv_mem hσ) (h b hb hQb)

/-! ### The generators act as $+1$ or $-1$ -/

/-- Helper: a symmetry $\tau_z$ in a vector $z \in L_\mathfrak p$ with $Q(z)$ a unit acts as $+1$ on the vectors of value
$\lvert\varpi\rvert$ (modulo $\mathfrak p\Lambda_p$), since $B(b,z) \in \mathfrak p$ for such $b$. -/
theorem DiagFrame.actsAs_symm_unit (hF : DiagFrame v Q L γ i j k) (h2 : (2 : 𝓞 F) ∉ v.asIdeal)
    (hint : ∀ x ∈ loc v L.1, Valued.v (Q.evalIn Fv x) ≤ 1) (haniso : ¬ Q.IsotropicIn Fv) {z : Fin 3 → Fv}
    (hz : z ∈ loc v L.1) (hQz : Valued.v (Q.evalIn Fv z) = 1) : ActsAs v Q L (symm Q Fv z) 1 := by
  intro b hb hQb
  have hb' : b ∈ locAct v γ (std v) := hF.basis ▸ hb
  have hz' : z ∈ locAct v γ (std v) := hF.basis ▸ hz
  obtain ⟨d, hd, rfl⟩ := mem_locAct.mp hb'
  obtain ⟨d', hd', rfl⟩ := mem_locAct.mp hz'
  obtain ⟨hi, hj, hk⟩ := hF.coords h2 hint haniso hd hQb
  have hz0 : Q.evalIn Fv (γ.val *ᵥ d') ≠ 0 := fun h => by rw [h, map_zero] at hQz; exact zero_ne_one hQz
  have hB : Valued.v (qbil Q Fv (γ.val *ᵥ d') (γ.val *ᵥ d)) ≤ exp (-1 : ℤ) := by
    rw [qbil_comm]; exact hF.bil_le hd' hi hj hk
  have hc : Valued.v (qbil Q Fv (γ.val *ᵥ d') (γ.val *ᵥ d) / Q.evalIn Fv (γ.val *ᵥ d')) ≤ exp (-1 : ℤ) := by
    rw [map_div₀, hQz, div_one]; exact hB
  have e : ((symm Q Fv (γ.val *ᵥ d') : GL (Fin 3) Fv)).val *ᵥ (γ.val *ᵥ d) - (1 : Fv) • (γ.val *ᵥ d) =
      -((qbil Q Fv (γ.val *ᵥ d') (γ.val *ᵥ d) / Q.evalIn Fv (γ.val *ᵥ d')) • (γ.val *ᵥ d')) := by
    rw [symm_mulVec_bil Q Fv hz0, one_smul]; abel
  rw [e]
  exact neg_mem_pLat L (smul_mem_pLat_of_le L hc hz)

/-- Helper: $Q(e_k)$ has valuation $\exp(-1)$. -/
theorem DiagFrame.valued_eval_k (hF : DiagFrame v Q L γ i j k) (h2 : (2 : 𝓞 F) ∉ v.asIdeal) :
    Valued.v (Q.evalIn Fv (γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single k 1)) = exp (-1 : ℤ) := by
  have h1 := two_mul_evalIn_eq Q Fv (γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single k 1)
  rw [locGram_apply_eq] at h1
  have := hF.vk
  rw [← h1, map_mul, valued_two h2, one_mul] at this
  exact this

/-- Helper: the symmetry $\tau_{e_k}$ in the vector of value $\lvert\varpi\rvert$ lies in $O(L_\mathfrak p)$, since
$\lvert B(e_k, y)\rvert \le \lvert Q(e_k)\rvert$ for $y \in L_\mathfrak p$. -/
theorem DiagFrame.symm_k_mem (hF : DiagFrame v Q L γ i j k) (h2 : (2 : 𝓞 F) ∉ v.asIdeal) :
    symm Q Fv (γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single k 1) ∈ locStabV Q v L := by
  have hE0 := hF.eval_ne_zero_k
  show locAct v (symm Q Fv (γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single k 1) : GL (Fin 3) Fv) (loc v L.1) = loc v L.1
  refine locAct_symm_eq (hF.single_mem k) hE0 fun y hy => ?_
  have hy' : y ∈ locAct v γ (std v) := hF.basis ▸ hy
  obtain ⟨d, hd, rfl⟩ := mem_locAct.mp hy'
  rw [qbil_single_eq hF.orth k d, hF.valued_eval_k h2, map_mul, hF.vk]
  calc exp (-1 : ℤ) * Valued.v (d k) ≤ exp (-1 : ℤ) * 1 := mul_le_mul' le_rfl ((mem_std_iff.mp hd) k)
    _ = _ := mul_one _

/-- Helper: the symmetry $\tau_{e_k}$ acts as $-1$ on the vectors of value $\lvert\varpi\rvert$ (modulo
$\mathfrak p\Lambda_p$): $\tau_{e_k}b = b - 2b_ke_k$ and $b \equiv b_ke_k$. -/
theorem DiagFrame.actsAs_symm_k (hF : DiagFrame v Q L γ i j k) (h2 : (2 : 𝓞 F) ∉ v.asIdeal)
    (hint : ∀ x ∈ loc v L.1, Valued.v (Q.evalIn Fv x) ≤ 1) (haniso : ¬ Q.IsotropicIn Fv) :
    ActsAs v Q L (symm Q Fv (γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single k 1)) (-1) := by
  intro b hb hQb
  have hb' : b ∈ locAct v γ (std v) := hF.basis ▸ hb
  obtain ⟨d, hd, rfl⟩ := mem_locAct.mp hb'
  obtain ⟨hi, hj, hk⟩ := hF.coords h2 hint haniso hd hQb
  have hE0 := hF.eval_ne_zero_k
  have h2v := valued_two h2
  have hQE : 2 * Q.evalIn Fv (γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single k 1) = locGram Q v γ k k := by
    rw [two_mul_evalIn_eq, locGram_apply_eq]
  have hc : qbil Q Fv (γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single k 1) (γ.val *ᵥ d) / Q.evalIn Fv (γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single k 1) =
      2 * d k := by
    rw [qbil_single_eq hF.orth k d, div_eq_iff hE0, ← hQE]; ring
  have e : ((symm Q Fv (γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single k 1) : GL (Fin 3) Fv)).val *ᵥ (γ.val *ᵥ d) - (-1 : Fv) • (γ.val *ᵥ d) =
      (2 * d i) • (γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single i 1) + (2 * d j) • (γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single j 1) := by
    rw [symm_mulVec_bil Q Fv hE0, hc, hF.decomp d]
    module
  rw [e]
  refine add_mem_pLat L (smul_mem_pLat_of_le L ?_ (hF.single_mem i)) (smul_mem_pLat_of_le L ?_ (hF.single_mem j))
  · rw [map_mul, h2v, one_mul]; exact hi
  · rw [map_mul, h2v, one_mul]; exact hj

/-! ### Generation of $O(L_\mathfrak p)$ -/

/-- Helper: **a variant of `exists_fix_step`.** If $\sigma \in O(L_\mathfrak p)$ fixes the orthogonal basis vectors $e_l$,
$l \in T$, and $Q(e_k)$ is a unit for an index $k \notin T$, there is a product $\rho$ of at most two unit symmetries in
$O(L_\mathfrak p)$ such that $\rho\sigma$ fixes $e_l$ for $l \in T$ and for $l = k$. (Same proof; only the diagonal entry
at $k$ is required to be a unit, and the set of fixed vectors is arbitrary instead of an initial segment.) -/
theorem exists_fix_step' (h2 : (2 : 𝓞 F) ∉ v.asIdeal) (L : Lat F 3) (γ : GL (Fin 3) Fv)
    (hγ : loc v L.1 = locAct v γ (std v)) (horth : ∀ a b, a ≠ b → locGram Q v γ a b = 0)
    (hint : ∀ x ∈ loc v L.1, Valued.v (Q.evalIn Fv x) ≤ 1) (k : Fin 3)
    (hunit : Valued.v (locGram Q v γ k k) = 1) (T : Set (Fin 3)) (hk : k ∉ T)
    (σ : orthGroup Q Fv) (hσ : σ ∈ locStabV Q v L)
    (hfix : ∀ l ∈ T, (σ : GL (Fin 3) Fv).val *ᵥ (γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single l 1) = γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single l 1) :
    ∃ ρ ∈ Subgroup.closure (unitSymmSet (Q := Q) (v := v) L), ρ ∈ locStabV Q v L ∧
      ∀ l : Fin 3, (l ∈ T ∨ l = k) →
        ((ρ * σ : orthGroup Q Fv) : GL (Fin 3) Fv).val *ᵥ (γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single l 1) =
          γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single l 1 := by
  have h2v : Valued.v (2 : Fv) = 1 := valued_two h2
  have h2ne : (2 : Fv) ≠ 0 := two_ne_zero
  set b : Fin 3 → Fv := γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single k 1 with hb
  set w : Fin 3 → Fv := (σ : GL (Fin 3) Fv).val *ᵥ b with hw
  have hmem : ∀ l, γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single l 1 ∈ loc v L.1 := fun l => by
    rw [hγ, mem_locAct]; exact ⟨_, single_mem_std l (by simp), rfl⟩
  have hbM : b ∈ loc v L.1 := hmem k
  have hσ' : locAct v (σ : GL (Fin 3) Fv) (loc v L.1) = loc v L.1 := hσ
  have hwM : w ∈ loc v L.1 := by
    rw [← hσ', mem_locAct]; exact ⟨b, hbM, rfl⟩
  have hQw : Q.evalIn Fv w = Q.evalIn Fv b := by
    apply mul_left_cancel₀ h2ne
    rw [two_mul_evalIn_eq, two_mul_evalIn_eq, hw]
    exact qbil_orth Q Fv σ b b
  have hQb : Valued.v (Q.evalIn Fv b) = 1 := by
    have : 2 * Q.evalIn Fv b = locGram Q v γ k k := by
      rw [two_mul_evalIn_eq, hb, locGram_apply_eq]
    have h := hunit
    rw [← this, map_mul, h2v, one_mul] at h
    exact h
  have hne : ∀ l ∈ T, k ≠ l := fun l hl h => hk (h ▸ hl)
  have hbl : ∀ l ∈ T, qbil Q Fv b (γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single l 1) = 0 := fun l hl => by
    rw [hb, locGram_apply_eq]; exact horth k l (hne l hl)
  have hwl : ∀ l ∈ T, qbil Q Fv w (γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single l 1) = 0 := fun l hl => by
    rw [hw]
    conv_lhs => rw [← hfix l hl]
    rw [qbil_orth Q Fv σ b _, hbl l hl]
  have hsymm_fix : ∀ z : Fin 3 → Fv, (∀ l ∈ T, qbil Q Fv z (γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single l 1) = 0) →
      ∀ l ∈ T, (symm Q Fv z : GL (Fin 3) Fv).val *ᵥ (γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single l 1) = γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single l 1 :=
    fun z hz l hl => symm_fix Q Fv (hz l hl)
  have hbS : symm Q Fv b ∈ Subgroup.closure (unitSymmSet (Q := Q) (v := v) L) :=
    Subgroup.subset_closure ⟨b, hbM, hQb, rfl⟩
  by_cases hA : Valued.v (Q.evalIn Fv (b - w)) = 1
  · have hz0 : Q.evalIn Fv (b - w) ≠ 0 := fun h => by rw [h, map_zero] at hA; exact zero_ne_one hA
    have hzM : b - w ∈ loc v L.1 := (loc v L.1).sub_mem hbM hwM
    refine ⟨symm Q Fv (b - w), Subgroup.subset_closure ⟨b - w, hzM, hA, rfl⟩,
      symm_mem_locStabV_of_unit L hint hzM hA, fun l hl => ?_⟩
    rw [coe_mul_mulVec]
    rcases hl with hl | rfl
    · rw [hfix l hl]
      exact hsymm_fix (b - w) (fun l hl => by rw [qbil_sub_left, hbl l hl, hwl l hl, sub_zero]) l hl
    · rw [← hb, ← hw]
      exact symm_sub_apply Q Fv hQw.symm hz0
  · have hlt : Valued.v (Q.evalIn Fv (b - w)) < 1 :=
      lt_of_le_of_ne (hint _ ((loc v L.1).sub_mem hbM hwM)) hA
    have hB : Valued.v (Q.evalIn Fv (b + w)) = 1 := by
      by_contra hB
      have hlt' : Valued.v (Q.evalIn Fv (b + w)) < 1 :=
        lt_of_le_of_ne (hint _ ((loc v L.1).add_mem hbM hwM)) hB
      have hsum := Valuation.map_add_lt _ hlt' hlt
      rw [parallelogram, hQw, ← mul_add, map_mul, h2v, one_mul] at hsum
      have : Q.evalIn Fv b + Q.evalIn Fv b = 2 * Q.evalIn Fv b := by ring
      rw [this, map_mul, h2v, one_mul, hQb] at hsum
      exact lt_irrefl _ hsum
    have hz0 : Q.evalIn Fv (b + w) ≠ 0 := fun h => by rw [h, map_zero] at hB; exact zero_ne_one hB
    have hzM : b + w ∈ loc v L.1 := (loc v L.1).add_mem hbM hwM
    have hzS : symm Q Fv (b + w) ∈ Subgroup.closure (unitSymmSet (Q := Q) (v := v) L) :=
      Subgroup.subset_closure ⟨b + w, hzM, hB, rfl⟩
    refine ⟨symm Q Fv b * symm Q Fv (b + w), Subgroup.mul_mem _ hbS hzS,
      (locStabV Q v L).mul_mem (symm_mem_locStabV_of_unit L hint hbM hQb)
        (symm_mem_locStabV_of_unit L hint hzM hB), fun l hl => ?_⟩
    rw [mul_assoc, coe_mul_mulVec, coe_mul_mulVec]
    rcases hl with hl | rfl
    · rw [hfix l hl, hsymm_fix (b + w) (fun l hl => by rw [qbil_add_left, hbl l hl, hwl l hl, add_zero]) l hl,
        hsymm_fix b hbl l hl]
    · have hQb0 : Q.evalIn Fv b ≠ 0 := fun h => by rw [h, map_zero] at hQb; exact zero_ne_one hQb
      rw [← hb, ← hw, symm_add_apply Q Fv hQw.symm hz0, symm_mulVec_bil Q Fv hQb0]
      have : qbil Q Fv b (-b) = -(2 * Q.evalIn Fv b) := by
        rw [qbil_comm, qbil_neg_left, qbil_self]
      rw [this, show -(2 * Q.evalIn Fv b) / Q.evalIn Fv b = -2 by field_simp]
      module

/-- Helper: an element of $O(V_\mathfrak p)$ that fixes all columns of $\gamma$ is the identity. -/
theorem eq_one_of_fix (γ : GL (Fin 3) Fv) {σ : orthGroup Q Fv}
    (h : ∀ l : Fin 3, (σ : GL (Fin 3) Fv).val *ᵥ (γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single l 1) = γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single l 1) :
    σ = 1 := by
  have h1 : (σ : GL (Fin 3) Fv) * γ = γ := by
    refine Units.ext (Matrix.ext fun a l => ?_)
    have := congrFun (h l) a
    rw [Matrix.mulVec_mulVec, Matrix.mulVec_single_one, Matrix.mulVec_single_one] at this
    exact this
  apply Subtype.ext
  exact (mul_left_inj γ).mp (h1.trans (one_mul γ).symm)

/-- Helper: **generators of $O(L_\mathfrak p)$.** In a diagonal frame, every element of $O(L_\mathfrak p)$ is a product of
symmetries $\tau_z$ with $z \in L_\mathfrak p$, $Q(z)$ a unit, and of the symmetry $\tau_{e_k}$ in the vector of value
$\lvert\varpi\rvert$. *Proof:* two steps of `exists_fix_step'` give a product $\rho$ of unit symmetries such that $\rho\sigma$
fixes the unit vectors $e_i, e_j$; then $\rho\sigma e_k$ is orthogonal to them with the value of $e_k$, so it is $\pm e_k$,
and $\rho\sigma$ or $\tau_{e_k}\rho\sigma$ fixes all of the basis, so is the identity. -/
theorem DiagFrame.mem_closure (hF : DiagFrame v Q L γ i j k) (h2 : (2 : 𝓞 F) ∉ v.asIdeal)
    (hint : ∀ x ∈ loc v L.1, Valued.v (Q.evalIn Fv x) ≤ 1) {σ : orthGroup Q Fv} (hσ : σ ∈ locStabV Q v L) :
    σ ∈ Subgroup.closure
      (insert (symm Q Fv (γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single k 1)) (unitSymmSet (Q := Q) (v := v) L)) := by
  have hmono : Subgroup.closure (unitSymmSet (Q := Q) (v := v) L) ≤
      Subgroup.closure (insert (symm Q Fv (γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single k 1)) (unitSymmSet (Q := Q) (v := v) L)) :=
    Subgroup.closure_mono (Set.subset_insert _ _)
  obtain ⟨ρ1, hρ1S, hρ1, hfix1⟩ := exists_fix_step' h2 L γ hF.basis hF.orth hint i hF.vi ∅
    (Set.notMem_empty i) σ hσ (fun l hl => absurd hl (Set.notMem_empty l))
  obtain ⟨ρ2, hρ2S, hρ2, hfix2⟩ := exists_fix_step' h2 L γ hF.basis hF.orth hint j hF.vj {i}
    (fun h => hF.ij (Set.mem_singleton_iff.mp h).symm) (ρ1 * σ) ((locStabV Q v L).mul_mem hρ1 hσ)
    (fun l hl => hfix1 l (Or.inr (Set.mem_singleton_iff.mp hl)))
  have hσ2 : ρ2 * (ρ1 * σ) ∈ locStabV Q v L := (locStabV Q v L).mul_mem hρ2 ((locStabV Q v L).mul_mem hρ1 hσ)
  have fi := hfix2 i (Or.inl (Set.mem_singleton i))
  have fj := hfix2 j (Or.inr rfl)
  have hE0 := hF.eval_ne_zero_k
  have hwM := mulVec_mem_loc hσ2 (hF.single_mem k)
  have hwM' : (((ρ2 * (ρ1 * σ) : orthGroup Q Fv)) : GL (Fin 3) Fv).val *ᵥ (γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single k 1) ∈
      locAct v γ (std v) := hF.basis ▸ hwM
  obtain ⟨c, -, hwc⟩ := mem_locAct.mp hwM'
  have hBi : locGram Q v γ i i * c i = 0 := by
    have := qbil_orth Q Fv (ρ2 * (ρ1 * σ)) (γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single i 1) (γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single k 1)
    rw [fi, ← hwc, qbil_single_eq hF.orth i c, locGram_apply_eq] at this
    rw [this]; exact hF.orth i k hF.ik
  have hBj : locGram Q v γ j j * c j = 0 := by
    have := qbil_orth Q Fv (ρ2 * (ρ1 * σ)) (γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single j 1) (γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single k 1)
    rw [fj, ← hwc, qbil_single_eq hF.orth j c, locGram_apply_eq] at this
    rw [this]; exact hF.orth j k hF.jk
  have hci : c i = 0 := (mul_eq_zero.mp hBi).resolve_left hF.ne_zero_i
  have hcj : c j = 0 := (mul_eq_zero.mp hBj).resolve_left hF.ne_zero_j
  have hck : c k * c k = 1 := by
    have := qbil_orth Q Fv (ρ2 * (ρ1 * σ)) (γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single k 1) (γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single k 1)
    rw [← hwc, hF.qbil_eq, hci, hcj, locGram_apply_eq] at this
    apply mul_left_cancel₀ hF.ne_zero_k
    linear_combination this
  have hcvec : c = c k • (Pi.single k 1 : Fin 3 → Fv) := by
    funext a
    rcases hF.cases a with rfl | rfl | rfl
    · simp [hci, hF.ik]
    · simp [hcj, hF.jk]
    · simp
  have hEk : (((ρ2 * (ρ1 * σ) : orthGroup Q Fv)) : GL (Fin 3) Fv).val *ᵥ (γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single k 1) =
      c k • (γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single k 1) := by
    rw [← hwc]
    conv_lhs => rw [hcvec]
    rw [Matrix.mulVec_smul]
  have hρ12 : ρ2 * ρ1 ∈ Subgroup.closure
      (insert (symm Q Fv (γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single k 1)) (unitSymmSet (Q := Q) (v := v) L)) :=
    Subgroup.mul_mem _ (hmono hρ2S) (hmono hρ1S)
  rcases mul_self_eq_one_iff.mp hck with h1 | h1
  · have hone : ρ2 * (ρ1 * σ) = 1 := by
      refine eq_one_of_fix γ fun l => ?_
      rcases hF.cases l with rfl | rfl | rfl
      · exact fi
      · exact fj
      · rw [hEk, h1, one_smul]
    have : σ = (ρ2 * ρ1)⁻¹ := eq_inv_of_mul_eq_one_right (by rw [mul_assoc]; exact hone)
    rw [this]
    exact Subgroup.inv_mem _ hρ12
  · have hone : symm Q Fv (γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single k 1) * (ρ2 * (ρ1 * σ)) = 1 := by
      refine eq_one_of_fix γ fun l => ?_
      rw [coe_mul_mulVec]
      rcases hF.cases l with rfl | rfl | rfl
      · rw [fi]
        exact symm_fix Q Fv (by rw [qbil_single_eq hF.orth k, Pi.single_eq_of_ne hF.ik.symm, mul_zero])
      · rw [fj]
        exact symm_fix Q Fv (by rw [qbil_single_eq hF.orth k, Pi.single_eq_of_ne hF.jk.symm, mul_zero])
      · rw [hEk, h1, neg_smul, one_smul]
        exact symm_neg_self Q Fv hE0
    have : σ = (symm Q Fv (γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single k 1) * (ρ2 * ρ1))⁻¹ :=
      eq_inv_of_mul_eq_one_right (by rw [mul_assoc, mul_assoc]; exact hone)
    rw [this]
    exact Subgroup.inv_mem _ (Subgroup.mul_mem _ (Subgroup.subset_closure (Set.mem_insert _ _)) hρ12)

/-- Helper: $-1 \ne 1$ in $F_\mathfrak p$ (characteristic $0$). -/
theorem neg_one_ne_one_loc : (-1 : Fv) ≠ 1 := fun h => by
  have : (2 : Fv) = 0 := by linear_combination (-1 : Fv) * h
  exact two_ne_zero this

/-- Helper: for $s, t \in \{1, -1\}$, $st = 1$ exactly when $s = 1 \leftrightarrow t = 1$. -/
theorem pm_mul_eq_one_iff {s t : Fv} (hs : s = 1 ∨ s = -1) (ht : t = 1 ∨ t = -1) :
    s * t = 1 ↔ (s = 1 ↔ t = 1) := by
  have hne := neg_one_ne_one_loc (v := v)
  rcases hs with rfl | rfl <;> rcases ht with rfl | rfl <;> simp [hne]

/-- Helper: **the sign of an element of $O(L_\mathfrak p)$.** In a diagonal frame, every $\sigma \in O(L_\mathfrak p)$ acts on
the vectors of value $\lvert\varpi\rvert$ (modulo $\mathfrak p\Lambda_p$) as $s \in \{1, -1\}$, and $s = 1$ exactly when
$\theta(\sigma)$ is a unit class. *Proof:* true for the generators of `DiagFrame.mem_closure` (`actsAs_symm_unit`,
`actsAs_symm_k`, with $\theta(\tau_z) = Q(z)$ and parity of the valuation), and the set of such $\sigma$ is closed under
products and inverses (`ActsAs.mul`, `ActsAs.inv`, `isUnitSqClass_mul_iff`). -/
theorem DiagFrame.exists_sign (hF : DiagFrame v Q L γ i j k) (h2 : (2 : 𝓞 F) ∉ v.asIdeal)
    (hint : ∀ x ∈ loc v L.1, Valued.v (Q.evalIn Fv x) ≤ 1) (haniso : ¬ Q.IsotropicIn Fv)
    (hQ : Q.Nondegenerate) {σ : orthGroup Q Fv} (hσ : σ ∈ locStabV Q v L) :
    ∃ s : Fv, (s = 1 ∨ s = -1) ∧ ActsAs v Q L σ s ∧ (IsUnitSqClass v (spinorNormHom Q Fv hQ σ) ↔ s = 1) := by
  have hpm : ∀ {s : Fv}, (s = 1 ∨ s = -1) → Valued.v s ≤ 1 ∧ s * s = 1 := by
    rintro s (rfl | rfl)
    · simp
    · simp [Valuation.map_neg]
  have key : ∀ τ ∈ Subgroup.closure
      (insert (symm Q Fv (γ.val *ᵥ Pi.single k 1)) (unitSymmSet (Q := Q) (v := v) L)),
      τ ∈ locStabV Q v L ∧ ∃ s : Fv, (s = 1 ∨ s = -1) ∧ ActsAs v Q L τ s ∧
        (IsUnitSqClass v (spinorNormHom Q Fv hQ τ) ↔ s = 1) := by
    intro τ hτ
    refine Subgroup.closure_induction (p := fun τ _ => τ ∈ locStabV Q v L ∧ ∃ s : Fv, (s = 1 ∨ s = -1) ∧
      ActsAs v Q L τ s ∧ (IsUnitSqClass v (spinorNormHom Q Fv hQ τ) ↔ s = 1)) ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_ hτ
    · intro x hx
      rcases hx with rfl | ⟨z, hz, hQz, rfl⟩
      · refine ⟨hF.symm_k_mem h2, -1, Or.inr rfl, hF.actsAs_symm_k h2 hint haniso, ?_⟩
        rw [spinorNormHom_apply, spinorNorm_symm Q Fv hQ hF.eval_ne_zero_k,
          isUnitSqClass_sqClassOf_iff hF.eval_ne_zero_k, hF.valued_eval_k h2, log_exp]
        exact ⟨fun h => absurd h (by decide), fun h => absurd h neg_one_ne_one_loc⟩
      · have hz0 : Q.evalIn Fv z ≠ 0 := fun h => by rw [h, map_zero] at hQz; exact zero_ne_one hQz
        refine ⟨symm_mem_locStabV_of_unit L hint hz hQz, 1, Or.inl rfl,
          hF.actsAs_symm_unit h2 hint haniso hz hQz, ?_⟩
        rw [spinorNormHom_apply, spinorNorm_symm Q Fv hQ hz0]
        exact ⟨fun _ => rfl, fun _ => ⟨_, hQz, rfl⟩⟩
    · refine ⟨(locStabV Q v L).one_mem, 1, Or.inl rfl, fun b _ _ => ?_, ?_⟩
      · simp [zero_mem_pLat]
      · rw [map_one]
        exact ⟨fun _ => rfl, fun _ => ⟨1, map_one _, sqClassOf_one.symm⟩⟩
    · rintro x y - - ⟨hx, s, hs, hxs, hxi⟩ ⟨hy, t, ht, hyt, hyi⟩
      refine ⟨(locStabV Q v L).mul_mem hx hy, s * t, ?_, hxs.mul hx (hpm ht).1 hyt, ?_⟩
      · rcases hs with rfl | rfl <;> rcases ht with rfl | rfl <;> simp
      · rw [map_mul, isUnitSqClass_mul_iff, hxi, hyi, pm_mul_eq_one_iff hs ht]
    · rintro x - ⟨hx, s, hs, hxs, hxi⟩
      refine ⟨(locStabV Q v L).inv_mem hx, s, hs, hxs.inv hx (hpm hs).2 (hpm hs).1, ?_⟩
      rw [map_inv, SqClass.inv_eq]
      exact hxi
  exact (key σ (hF.mem_closure h2 hint hσ)).2

end DiagFrame

/-! ### Example 2 -/

section Example2

variable (Q : QuadForm F 3)

/-- Helper: **a diagonal frame exists** under the hypotheses of Example 1: integer-valued form on the ternary lattice
$L_\mathfrak p = \gamma\,\mathfrak o_\mathfrak p^3$ with $\lvert\det(\gamma^tH\gamma)\rvert = \lvert\varpi\rvert$. Diagonalize
(`exists_diag_basis`): the three diagonal entries have valuations $\exp(-\nu_a)$ with $\sum\nu_a = 1$, so two are
units and one has valuation $\exp(-1)$. Here `hQ` is nondegeneracy of `Q`, `h2` that $\mathfrak p \nmid 2$, `L` the lattice,
`γ` a basis of its localization (`hγ`), `hint` integrality and `hdet` the determinant condition. -/
theorem exists_diagFrame (hQ : Q.Nondegenerate) (h2 : (2 : 𝓞 F) ∉ v.asIdeal) (L : Lat F 3) (γ : GL (Fin 3) Fv)
    (hγ : loc v L.1 = locAct v γ (std v)) (hint : ∀ x ∈ loc v L.1, Valued.v (Q.evalIn Fv x) ≤ 1)
    (hdet : Valued.v (locGram Q v γ).det = exp (-1 : ℤ)) :
    ∃ (γ' : GL (Fin 3) Fv) (i j k : Fin 3), DiagFrame v Q L γ' i j k := by
  obtain ⟨γ', ν, hγ', horth, hval, hdet'⟩ := exists_diag_basis hQ h2 L γ hγ hint
  have hG : locGram Q v γ' = Matrix.diagonal (fun k => locGram Q v γ' k k) := by
    ext k l
    by_cases h : k = l
    · subst h; simp
    · rw [horth k l h, Matrix.diagonal_apply_ne _ h]
  have hd1 := hdet'.trans hdet
  rw [hG, Matrix.det_diagonal, map_prod] at hd1
  simp only [hval] at hd1
  rw [prod_exp, exp_inj] at hd1
  have h3 : (∑ k, ν k) = 1 := by
    have : (∑ k, -(ν k : ℤ)) = -((∑ k, ν k : ℕ) : ℤ) := by simp [Finset.sum_neg_distrib]
    omega
  rw [Fin.sum_univ_three] at h3
  have hv0 : ∀ k, ν k = 0 → Valued.v (locGram Q v γ' k k) = 1 := fun k hk => by
    rw [hval k, hk]; simp
  have hv1 : ∀ k, ν k = 1 → Valued.v (locGram Q v γ' k k) = exp (-1 : ℤ) := fun k hk => by
    rw [hval k, hk]; simp
  have a0 : ν 0 = 1 ∧ ν 1 = 0 ∧ ν 2 = 0 ∨ ν 0 = 0 ∧ ν 1 = 1 ∧ ν 2 = 0 ∨ ν 0 = 0 ∧ ν 1 = 0 ∧ ν 2 = 1 := by
    omega
  rcases a0 with ⟨h0, h1, h2'⟩ | ⟨h0, h1, h2'⟩ | ⟨h0, h1, h2'⟩
  · exact ⟨γ', 1, 2, 0, ⟨hγ', horth, by decide, by decide, by decide, hv0 _ h1, hv0 _ h2', hv1 _ h0⟩⟩
  · exact ⟨γ', 0, 2, 1, ⟨hγ', horth, by decide, by decide, by decide, hv0 _ h0, hv0 _ h2', hv1 _ h1⟩⟩
  · exact ⟨γ', 0, 1, 2, ⟨hγ', horth, by decide, by decide, by decide, hv0 _ h0, hv0 _ h1, hv1 _ h2'⟩⟩

/-- **Cassels, Ch. 10, Example 2** (p. 192), for all of $O(\Lambda_p)$. Notation and hypotheses as in Example 1
(`localSpinorNormGroup_eq_top_of_det`): $\mathfrak p \nmid 2$ (`h2`), `Q` nondegenerate (`hQ`) on $F^3$, `L` a lattice with
the basis `γ` of its localization $\Lambda_p = L_\mathfrak p$ (`hγ`), $Q$ integer-valued on $\Lambda_p$ (`hint`), and the
determinant of the form induced on $\Lambda_p$ of valuation exactly $\exp(-1)$, i.e. divisible by $p$ but not by $p^2$
(`hdet`). Suppose also that $V_\mathfrak p$ is anisotropic (`haniso`). Let `b` be any element of $\Lambda_p$ with
$\lvert Q(b)\rvert_\mathfrak p = \lvert\varpi\rvert$ (`hb`, `hQb`) and `σ` any element of $O(\Lambda_p)$ (`hσ`). Then
$\sigma b \equiv \varepsilon b \pmod{\mathfrak p\Lambda_p}$, where $\varepsilon = +1$ if $\theta(\sigma)$ is a unit class (first
conclusion) and $\varepsilon = -1$ if $\theta(\sigma)$ is the class of $\varpi u$, $u$ a unit (second conclusion); every
square class is one of the two (`isUnitSqClass_or_uniformizer`). *Proof:* see the module docstring. -/
@[kb "cassels1978" "Ch. 10, Example 2, p. 192 (generalization: number field; all of O(Λ_p))"]
theorem ch10_example2_orth (hQ : Q.Nondegenerate) (h2 : (2 : 𝓞 F) ∉ v.asIdeal) (L : Lat F 3) (γ : GL (Fin 3) Fv)
    (hγ : loc v L.1 = locAct v γ (std v)) (hint : ∀ x ∈ loc v L.1, Valued.v (Q.evalIn Fv x) ≤ 1)
    (hdet : Valued.v (locGram Q v γ).det = exp (-1 : ℤ)) (haniso : ¬ Q.IsotropicIn Fv)
    {σ : orthGroup Q Fv} (hσ : σ ∈ locStabV Q v L) {b : Fin 3 → Fv} (hb : b ∈ loc v L.1)
    (hQb : Valued.v (Q.evalIn Fv b) = exp (-1 : ℤ)) :
    (IsUnitSqClass v (spinorNorm Q Fv σ) → (σ : GL (Fin 3) Fv).val *ᵥ b - b ∈ pLat v L) ∧
    ((∃ u : Fv, Valued.v u = 1 ∧ spinorNorm Q Fv σ = sqClassOf (((LocalDensity.NF.π v : 𝔬) : Fv) * u)) →
      (σ : GL (Fin 3) Fv).val *ᵥ b + b ∈ pLat v L) := by
  obtain ⟨γ', i, j, k, hF⟩ := exists_diagFrame v Q hQ h2 L γ hγ hint hdet
  obtain ⟨s, hs, hact, hiff⟩ := hF.exists_sign h2 hint haniso hQ hσ
  rw [spinorNormHom_apply] at hiff
  have hab := hact b hb hQb
  refine ⟨fun hU => ?_, fun ⟨u, hu, hθ⟩ => ?_⟩
  · rw [hiff.mp hU, one_smul] at hab
    exact hab
  · have hnU : ¬ IsUnitSqClass v (spinorNorm Q Fv σ) := by
      rw [hθ]; exact not_isUnitSqClass_uniformizer_mul hu
    rw [hs.resolve_left fun h => hnU (hiff.mpr h), neg_smul, one_smul, sub_neg_eq_add] at hab
    exact hab

/-- **Cassels, Ch. 10, Example 2** (p. 192). Notation and hypotheses as in Example 1: $\mathfrak p \nmid 2$ (`h2`),
`Q` nondegenerate (`hQ`) on $F^3$, `L` a lattice with the basis `γ` of $\Lambda_p = L_\mathfrak p$ (`hγ`), $Q$ integer-valued
on $\Lambda_p$ (`hint`), and the determinant of the form induced on $\Lambda_p$ of valuation exactly $\exp(-1)$ (`hdet`).
Suppose also that $V_\mathfrak p$ is anisotropic (`haniso`). Let `b` be any element of $\Lambda_p$ with
$\lvert Q(b)\rvert_\mathfrak p = \lvert\varpi\rvert$ (`hb`, `hQb`) and `σ` any element of $O^+(\Lambda_p)$ (`hσ`). Then
$\sigma b \equiv \varepsilon b \pmod{\mathfrak p\Lambda_p}$ with $\varepsilon = +1$ if $\theta(\sigma)$ is in $U_p(\mathbb Q_p^\times)^2$
(a unit class; first conclusion) and $\varepsilon = -1$ if $\theta(\sigma)$ is in $\varpi U_p(\mathbb Q_p^\times)^2$ (the class of
$\varpi u$, $u$ a unit; second conclusion). -/
@[kb "cassels1978" "Ch. 10, Example 2, p. 192 (generalization: number field)"]
theorem ch10_example2 (hQ : Q.Nondegenerate) (h2 : (2 : 𝓞 F) ∉ v.asIdeal) (L : Lat F 3) (γ : GL (Fin 3) Fv)
    (hγ : loc v L.1 = locAct v γ (std v)) (hint : ∀ x ∈ loc v L.1, Valued.v (Q.evalIn Fv x) ≤ 1)
    (hdet : Valued.v (locGram Q v γ).det = exp (-1 : ℤ)) (haniso : ¬ Q.IsotropicIn Fv)
    {σ : orthGroup Q Fv} (hσ : σ ∈ locStabV Q v L ⊓ Tamagawa.soSub Q Fv) {b : Fin 3 → Fv}
    (hb : b ∈ loc v L.1) (hQb : Valued.v (Q.evalIn Fv b) = exp (-1 : ℤ)) :
    (IsUnitSqClass v (spinorNorm Q Fv σ) → (σ : GL (Fin 3) Fv).val *ᵥ b - b ∈ pLat v L) ∧
    ((∃ u : Fv, Valued.v u = 1 ∧ spinorNorm Q Fv σ = sqClassOf (((LocalDensity.NF.π v : 𝔬) : Fv) * u)) →
      (σ : GL (Fin 3) Fv).val *ᵥ b + b ∈ pLat v L) :=
  ch10_example2_orth v Q hQ h2 L γ hγ hint hdet haniso hσ.1 hb hQb

end Example2

